---
title: "One O channel with a per-channel execution node, issue 8486"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Unmanaged
    lg1: Designated
    lg2: Moving
    lg3: Breaks BusyTurnFinishes
    lg4: Path to the BusyTurnFinishes bug
  }
  class lg0 tan
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 pink
  class lg3 breaks
  class lg4 bugPath
  s0: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set)
  s1: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node)
  s2: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway
  s3: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input is kept for the designated node
  s4: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node), an input is handed to the designated node
  s5: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node), turn runs on the designated node
  s6: Home is the designated node (no node set), turn runs on the designated node
  s7: Home is the designated node (no node set), an input waits at the gateway, turn runs on the designated node
  s8: Home is the designated node (no node set), an input is kept for the gateway, turn runs on the designated node
  s9: Home is the designated node (no node set), an input is kept for the gateway, old home asked to end, turn runs on the designated node
  s10: Home is the designated node (no node set), an input is kept for the gateway, old home ended [busy turn cut]
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s0: an operator edits one node's config file
  s0 --> s1: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s1 --> s1: an operator edits one node's config file
  s1 --> s2: you send a message
  s2 --> s3: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s3 --> s4: the input is handed to the node that owns the channel
  s4 --> s4: a node reads the owner row again
  s4 --> s5: the home starts the turn
  s5 --> s6: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s6 --> s7: you send a message
  s7 --> s8: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s8 --> s9: the old home is asked to end its session
  s9 --> s10: the old home answers the request
